*.egg-info/
# A built wheel, anywhere. `dist/` already covers the ordinary case — `python -m build` writes
# there — but a `pip wheel .` or a `--outdir .` puts one at the repository ROOT, outside every
# rule above, and one sat there untracked across five rounds: `synapse_cdm-1.0.0-py3-none-any.whl`,
# one `git add -A` from being committed. Committing a wheel would break
# `tests/test_cdm_packaging.py` and `gates/wheel_install.py`, which compare a BUILT wheel's
# manifest against `git ls-files` in both directions — a tracked wheel makes the artefact part of
# its own input. The rule is the extension and not the one filename, for the reason the archive
# block below gives about itself: a `.whl` is never an artefact this repository tracks, so the rule
# costs nothing and the next stray one does not get to be the test case.
*.whl
.DS_Store

# Documentation site (Docusaurus)
docs/node_modules/
docs/build/
docs/.docusaurus/
docs/.cache-loader/
.wrangler/

# Pinned specification documents. NEVER COMMITTED — and until this block existed that was true
# by discipline plus a test, which is a gate on the COMMIT and not on the operation.
#
# THE FAILURE THIS CLOSES. `tests/test_cdm_pins.py::test_no_pdf_is_tracked_anywhere_in_the_
# repository` asserts `git ls-files` returns no `.pdf` anywhere. It is a good gate and it fires
# after the fact: `git add -A` from the repository root stages all 52 held documents, and only a
# suite run or a reading of `git status` catches it before the commit. That near-miss has happened
# twice. The rule below makes the staging itself refuse, so the gate and the mechanism now fail in
# the same direction and neither is load-bearing alone.
#
# THE EXTENSION SET IS DERIVED, NOT GUESSED. Every file under a `fixtures/*/spec/` directory is a
# `.pdf` (52), a `.json` pin record (8) or a `.py` generator (8), and the last two are exactly the
# committed artefacts — which is why this ignores an EXTENSION and not the `spec/` directory. A
# `spec/` rule would hide the pin records, and the pin record is the whole point of pinning.
*.pdf

#
# THOSE THREE COUNTS WERE 36 / 6 / 5 AND WERE STALE, corrected 2026-08-26 by the STANAG 4609
# round's sweep. They had drifted as the CAT023, CAT034, CAT048 and CAT062 lineages landed, because
# nothing sends anybody back to a comment in this file. The load-bearing half — that the extension
# set is exactly those three and no other — was and is true, so the RULE never stopped working;
# only the arithmetic beside it went wrong. Recorded rather than quietly fixed, because a number
# that describes itself as derived and is in fact typed is precisely the claim a disjunction sweep
# exists to catch. It is derived by:
#   find packages/cdm/synapse_cdm/fixtures -type f -path '*/spec/*' | sed 's/.*\.//' | sort | uniq -c
#
# THE GENERATOR COUNT MOVED FROM 5 TO 7 TO 8, and the third move is the first one that was not a
# repair. The KLV framing round of 2026-08-26 added `fixtures/klv/spec/build_fixtures.py`, so the
# count went stale the moment the file landed and was corrected in the same commit — which is the
# discipline the paragraph above asks for, applied by the round that created the drift instead of by
# a later sweep that found it. The extension SET did not change and the rule did not move.
#
# THE PDF COUNT MOVED FROM 47 TO 48 on 2026-08-26, by the KLV length round, which obtained MISB
# ST 0107.3 and pinned it at `fixtures/klv/spec/ST0107.3.pdf`. Corrected in the same commit that
# created the drift, which is what the paragraph above asks for and is the second time it has been
# done that way rather than left to a later sweep. The extension SET did not change and the rule did
# not move. Worth noting that this is the count the rule EXISTS for: the 48th document is a six-page
# free download that closed a park, so the number grows every time somebody does the cheap thing.
#
# THE PDF COUNT MOVED FROM 48 TO 52 on 2026-08-26, by the KLV park 13 adjudication round, which
# obtained four editions of the MISB 0601 series: EG 0601.1 as a PIN at
# `fixtures/klv/spec/EG0601.1.pdf` — the document that closed park 13 — and the initial release,
# ST 0601.4 and ST 0601.8 as the 0601 LINEAGE at `fixtures/klv/spec/history/`. Corrected in the same
# commit that created the drift, which is the third time it has been done that way rather than left
# to a later sweep. The extension SET did not change and the rule did not move.
#
# THIS ROUND ALSO ADDED THE FIFTH `spec/history/` DIRECTORY, and that is worth a line because the
# rule above is an EXTENSION rule and therefore did not need to notice. `fixtures/klv/spec/history/`
# joins cat023's, cat034's, cat048's and cat062's; `git check-ignore -v` was run on each of the four
# files that landed and each reports `.gitignore:42:*.pdf`, so the citation to that LINE still holds.
# A `spec/`-directory rule would have needed editing here; an extension rule did not, which is the
# argument the derived-set paragraph above makes about itself.
#
# THIS NOTE SITS BELOW THE RULE AND NOT ABOVE IT, deliberately. `*.pdf` is cited as `.gitignore:42`
# in `klv_pin.json` and in commit messages, and a citation to a LINE is only worth having if the
# line holds still — so a comment added above the rule would have silently re-pointed every one of
# those citations at a blank line. The correction goes underneath.


# Archives, because that is how a lineage arrives. `cat048_pin.json` records `bundle_url` as
# `https://www.eurocontrol.int/archive_download/all/node/11127` under the link text "Download all"
# — the 22-edition CAT048 lineage came down as one archive. Only `.zip` is evidenced by that
# record; the siblings are listed because they are the same class with the same failure mode and
# none of them is ever an artefact of this repository, so the rule costs nothing and the next
# publisher who serves a tarball does not get to be the test case.
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
fixtures/klv/streams/

# Fetched provenance evidence, because that is how a HELD file's origin gets established.
#
# `fixtures/klv/provenance/` holds what the Day Flight provenance round of 2026-08-26 fetched to
# answer one question about a file this repository already had: where did the pinned transport
# stream come from. The answer is byte identity against a served copy, and reaching it took Wayback
# CDX index dumps, archived pages of the MISB's own website, that site's machine-readable
# publication catalogues, and the sample collection's directory listings and index. All of it is
# EVIDENCE for sentences in FORMAT_COVERAGE.md and none of it is an artefact this repository ships.
#
# A DIRECTORY RULE AND NOT AN EXTENSION RULE, for the reason the `fixtures/klv/streams/` block
# above gives about itself and more so. The PDF rule works because a `spec/` directory holds three
# known extensions and a new document is the ordinary case. Fetched evidence has no extension
# discipline at all: this round alone landed `.txt` CDX dumps, `.html` archived pages, `.xml` site
# catalogues and one extensionless `00-README`, and the next round could just as well hold `.json`,
# `.warc` or a bare header dump. An extension rule would be a list somebody has to remember to
# extend, and the failure mode of forgetting is that somebody else's website enters the index.
#
# WHY NOT JUST LEAVE IT IN A TEMPORARY DIRECTORY. Because the standing rule is that every asserted
# fact comes from bytes HELD and PINNED, and a quotation from a page that was read and thrown away
# is a recollection. Each file here is pinned by SHA-256 and byte count in `klv_pin.json` under
# `day_flight_provenance_2026_08_26`, with the origin URL it was served from, exactly as the PDFs
# are. `git check-ignore -v` was run on every file that landed and each reports this rule.
fixtures/klv/provenance/
